    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d561">

                <pb facs="0982" n="878" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg878"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt
                    Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Roosevelt</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d561-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-03-09">9 March 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>613. Prime Minister to President Roosevelt. Personal and secret.…<anchor n="2" xml:id="d561-f2"/></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>You will remember that we discussed the dollar balances in Cairo on
                        December 8th and that I gave a memorandum to Harry.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d561-f3"/>
                        <pb facs="0983" n="879" xml:id="pg879"/> I certainly understood that you
                        felt we ought not to be treated worse than France or Russia in these
                        matters.…</item>
                </list>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d561-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d561-f1-content">
                <p>Presumably sent via military channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d561-f2" n="2" xml:id="d561-f2-content">
                <p>For the full text of this telegram, see Churchill, <ref target="#pg697">p. 697</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d561-f3" n="3" xml:id="d561-f3-content">
                <p>Roosevelt left Cairo on the morning of
                    December 7, 1943. For what is believed to be the memorandum given to Harry Hopkins, see <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg822">p. 822</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
